course: dictionary
lesson: 10403
title: Trickery and tricking
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Trickery means using tricks to fool people, or to make them believe something that is not true. «Israel's leaders were tricked by the Gibeonites into a treaty but kept it.» The word tricked tells you the leaders were fooled, so trickery is the sneaky way it was done.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Trickery is about deceiving someone on purpose, so the person using it wants you to believe something false. Check your meaning by swapping in "lies and sneaky tricks" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Trickery can also be fun. In magic shows and films, "camera trickery" makes things look real when they are not, like a dragon or a flying car. Nobody is being cheated here: the audience knows it is an illusion and enjoys being fooled.
explain: The same word can be bad or good depending on the situation. A sly fox in a story uses trickery to cheat others, but a magician uses trickery to entertain. Ask yourself: is someone being cheated, or is everyone in on the fun?
fact: Trickery is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say "a bit of trickery", not "a trickery".
fact: Trickery means using tricks to deceive or cheat people.
fact: «He won the game by trickery.» means he won by cheating, not fairly.
fact: «Camera trickery» means special effects that fool the eye on purpose, for fun.
fact: Online scammers use trickery, such as fake messages and fake websites, so always check before you click.
exercise: «Israel's leaders were tricked by the Gibeonites into a treaty.» What does the word tricked tell you? | The leaders were very happy | *The leaders were fooled | The leaders were given a prize | The leaders went for a walk
exercise: «Camera trickery» is used in films. What is camera trickery? | Recording people's voices | *Special effects that fool the eye for fun | A new camera that takes better photos | Filming in the dark
exercise: Which word means using tricks to cheat people? | *Trickery | Sunshine | Patience | Kindness
test: «Trickery» is most like which word? | *Deceit | Honesty | Kindness
test: Which is a fun use of trickery? | A fox tricking the hens | Lying to get money | A scammer's fake message | *A magician's trick that makes a rabbit seem to vanish
exam: Which sentence uses trickery to mean a fun illusion? | The boy was caught in trickery and lies. | The scammer used trickery to steal her password. | *The film used camera trickery to make the dragon look real. | The fox used trickery to steal the hens.
